  "findings": [
    "The push trigger is restricted to the intended research branch and the workflow/request paths. The first executable gate requires run_attempt1, the expected before-commit, the actual after-commit, the exact branch, one permitted native preparation, zero optimizer calls, no retry and the frozen model dimensions.",
    "All59 sparse-checkout paths were compared as an exact set against all34 configured inputs,3 helper sources,3 proof files,11 review records, producer, driver, configuration, workflow, gate/request and the2 new independent review paths. No required path is missing and no extra path is present.",
    "All three actions are pinned to full immutable commits. Permissions are contents:read and actions:read; checkout credentials are not persisted. The workflow does not commit, push or send external messages.",
    "Every gate dependency is byte/hash-checked and every pinned Python dependency is compiled before the installed-runtime/native phases. The configuration and source/gate/request references are then independently checked by the driver before calls and protected dependencies are checked again after successful cold replay.",
    "The one producer controls/prepare sequence and separate checker controls/replay sequence use the exact accepted CLI/status contracts. Six fresh, disjoint worker/owner directories are required. Producer and checker owners require successful child exit, process-group reaping/stopping and no deadline overrun; a PASS-shaped report alone is insufficient.",
    "Worker/owner allowances are10/15seconds for each controls phase and120/135seconds for each main phase. The driver checks its420-second budget and rejects a final overrun; the GitHub preparation job has a12-minute timeout. No CpSolver query exists in this workflow or driver.",
    "The complete preparation raw-model hash/length must agree with the independent cold. The cold must also recover the exact original38,374,405-byte parent with SHA4a9b24ab... . No native model is accepted from archive-export success alone.",
    "The small log bundle base64-encodes the exact original bytes of every selected report/receipt/log/patch/suffix; it does not parse or reserialize the control report containing the integer above2^53. Original small binary artifacts, partial reports and error/owner records are included when present, with explicit16MiB raw and12MiB encoded bounds.",
    "The complete artifact upload includes all six directories, full raw/compressed model, runtime package inventory and top-level driver logs/result. Export and upload steps are configured to run after ordinary preceding-step failures; execution success and artifact availability remain outcomes to be observed.",
    "The three archive-export jobs only read the saved artifact. They check the complete archive against its actual preparation report and emit exact bounded4MiB chunks with per-chunk and complete hashes, offsets and lengths. Empty terminal chunks are explicit. The headers mark export as distinct from model acceptance, and the12MiB archive cap prevents silent truncation."
